// pricing-card-variants-2.jsx — Pricing Performance redesign with correct
// Amazon / Bookzy terminology + priority weighting.
//
// Updated facts:
//   • "High Pricing Alerts" — exact Amazon term. SKUs Amazon flags as
//     priced too high and INACTIVATES. Red. Higher priority.
//   • "Global Min Reach" — Bookzy's own feature. User sets a minimum
//     payout limit; when an SKU's payout hits that floor its price
//     can't go lower. Usually cheap items. Amber. Lower priority.
//   • Never say "catalog" — sellers say "inventory".
//
// These two roles should NOT have equal visual weight (the prior round
// showed them equal). High Pricing Alerts must read as the primary state;
// Global Min Reach as the supporting one.

