// orders-screen.jsx — Orders tab. PRD: today's sales activity.
//
// Layout (top → bottom):
//   1. Large title "Orders" + dated subtitle ("Today · Mon May 26")
//   2. Daily performance summary card
//        Hero: today's revenue in display weight, "Items sold" caption.
//        Below: 2×2 grid of secondary metrics
//          (Avg price · Avg payout · Est. total payout · Est. per-unit payout)
//        Revenue uses the sales accent (orange = sales context, per design system)
//        Hairline divider between hero and the secondary grid.
//   3. Sort + Filter chip-buttons row. Each shows active state with a count.
//   4. Sales list — cards-as-rows in a CardGroup (iOS list pattern).
//        Row layout:
//          [thumb 60×60]  TITLE                         $PRICE
//                         SKU · meta-row                Sold in 3d
//                                                       Rank #84,231
//   5. Floating scroll-to-top button when scrolled.
//
// Design moves:
//   • Hero revenue gets the only orange accent — anchors the page as
//     "sales today" and tonally separates it from Home's neutral cards.
//   • Per-row sale price (the row's headline) is in display font + bold
//     so the eye scans the right edge as a money column.
//   • "Days listed" is quiet ash gray; "Sold in 3d" sits next to the
//     price using a fresh-leaf success tone — celebrates fast sales
//     subtly without becoming a badge.
//   • Channel + condition badges use the StatusPill component, paired
//     so the row's chip cluster always reads in the same order.
//
// Data: 9 fabricated sample orders covering FBA/FBM, all conditions,
// and a spread of price/sold-in/age values so the page is visually
// interesting.

