// scan-screen.jsx — Scan tab. PRD: tools & preferences hub + session launcher.
//
// Layout (top → bottom):
//   1. Large title "Scanner" + subtitle
//   2. Launch hero — combined active-mode + primary CTA.
//        The page's job is to start a session, so the launcher is hero.
//        Inside the card:
//          - "Scanner mode" eyebrow
//          - Mode name (Legacy / Pro) + optional Beta chip
//          - One-line description of the active mode
//          - Quiet "Change mode" link (→ Scan Settings)
//          - Full-width primary CTA: "Start scanning"
//   3. Configuration — CardGroup of 3 Rows:
//        - Local database  → "Updated 3 hr ago"
//        - Triggers        → "8 total · 5 active"
//        - Scan settings   → buy cost as the trailing value (e.g. "$3.50")
//
// Design moves:
//   • Launch panel is the hero. It's the only thing on the page that
//     uses primary color — every other surface is the neutral card style.
//   • The mode line uses a tinted pill (purple for Pro/Beta, neutral for
//     Legacy) so the mode is identifiable at a glance.
//   • Rows borrow the same icon-tile + chevron pattern used elsewhere in
//     the app (Row component) so this page feels native to the rest.

